    "author_association": "OWNER",
    "body": "OWNER_ACTION_SCENE_DIRECTIVE_R03 — BLADE-DODGE PRODUCTION BACKGROUND\n\nSOURCE = OWNER directive in active ZORR session, 2026-08-30\nMAIN_HEAD_OBSERVED = b18ca6b9cce2dce6fe304ca8ae36c05df4f4dcb1\nSTATE = VISIBLE LOCAL 3D PROTOTYPE / NOT BABYLON PASS / NOT CANON\n\nOWNER REQUIREMENT:\n- background must be usable for further production, not a decorative flat image;\n- build the scene only, no 2D drawing/imitation;\n- action = one actor attacks with a blade, second actor visibly dodges the strike.\n\nR03 VISIBLE PRODUCT SLICE:\n- real OxiHuman-derived body-only surface, 14,517 vertices / 26,756 triangles per actor;\n- two actual 3D actor meshes;\n- modular brutalist production-greybox set: physical floor, segmented rear wall, deep opening, columns, beams, step, floor seams, practical-light geometry;\n- real 3D blade + grip + crossguard geometry;\n- perspective camera + actual scene lights;\n- upper-body dodge/lunge produced by smooth 3D vertex deformation while preserving common ground contact; no PIL/2D character construction.\n\nACTION MATH:\n- attacker = translation [-0.62,0,0.05] m, yaw -8°, upper-body lean +0.16 m toward opponent;\n- dodger = translation [0.62,0,-0.05] m, yaw +15°, upper-body lateral dodge +0.34 m;\n- blade length = 1.08 m;\n- blade segment is solved from attacker's measured donor right-hand region toward a near-miss point beside the dodger's head/neck;\n- minimum sampled blade-to-dodger surface-vertex clearance = 0.0970096418 m (~9.7 cm), so the strike reads as a miss rather than penetration;\n- both actors share the same physical ground plane.\n\nCAMERA:\n- resolution = 1280x720;\n- position = [3.10, 1.55, 3.65] m;\n- target = [0.12, 1.02, -0.38] m;\n- vertical FOV = 39°.\n\nRENDER:\n- local renderer = VTK 9.6.2 real 3D rasterization;\n- SSAO + FXAA enabled;\n- offscreen shadow mapping disabled because the current headless path produced unstable/over-dark captures; no fake painted shadows substituted;\n- final PNG SHA256 = 91847b1e9ade368c70d42b8c304fe62e9c7090eee572c0a35d8034c4d5b3577f.\n\nIMPORTANT BOUNDARY:\nThis R03 frame is an immediate visible scene/blocking prototype and records the OWNER's new action/background direction. It does NOT claim Babylon branch update, Babylon CI PASS, independent DUNCAN QC, merge, canon, character truth, or production activation.\n\nNEXT PRODUCT STEP = port this exact action/set/camera intent into the Babylon scene path, preserving measured actor/blade/camera geometry and replacing only the temporary local renderer boundary.",
